      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "step-start",
          "id": "prt_0f747eb6d001PGwVdgz75m7RM2",
          "sessionID": "ses_f08b84bc6ffejyKgRPZNOHpExE",
          "messageID": "msg_0f747da7c001LEK1VXk8cd4kUF"
        },
        {
          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "The bug: `<=` makes touching intervals overlap, and empty intervals like [3,3) and [4,4): max(3,4)=4 <= min(3,4)=3 → False. But [3,3) and [2,5): max(3,2)=3 <= min(3,5)=3 → True, incorrectly (empty interval should not overlap). Fix: change `<=` to `<`. Half-open intervals overlap iff max(starts) < min(ends). Check empty: [3,3) vs [2,5): 3 < 3 → False. Good. Touching [0,2) and [2,4): 2 < 2 → False. Good. Genuinely overlapping [0,3) and [2,4): 2 < 3 → True. Disjoint [0,1) and [3,5): 3 < 1 → False. Good.",
          "time": {
            "start": 1790855080816,
            "end": 1790855087060
          },
          "id": "prt_0f747eb70001d3DVJark998TxM",
          "sessionID": "ses_f08b84bc6ffejyKgRPZNOHpExE",
          "messageID": "msg_0f747da7c001LEK1VXk8cd4kUF"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "{\"action\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"intervals.py\",\"old\":\"    return max(left[0], right[0]) <= min(left[1], right[1])\",\"new\":\"    return max(left[0], right[0]) < min(left[1], right[1])\"}",
          "time": {
            "start": 1790855087062,
            "end": 1790855087312
