        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "{\"action\":\"finish\",\"answer\":\"Fixed `overlaps` in intervals.py: half-open intervals [start, end) overlap iff max(starts) < min(ends), not <=. The previous `<=` incorrectly reported touching intervals (e.g., [0,2) and [2,4)) and empty intervals (e.g., [3,3) and [2,5)) as overlapping. With strict `<`: touching intervals ([0,2), [2,4)) → False; empty intervals ([3,3) vs anything) → False since max(starts) >= min(ends); genuinely overlapping ([0,3), [2,4)) → True; disjoint ([0,1), [3,5)) → False. Public API unchanged (overlaps, span untouched). Source: intervals.py, `overlaps` function, line `return max(left[0], right[0]) < min(left[1], right[1])`.\"}",
          "time": {
            "start": 1790855092070,
            "end": 1790855097197
